## 3. For CRM / Lifecycle / Retention Leaders

### Headline

**Move the metrics your stack already optimizes — through the surface it can't reach anymore.**

### Subheadline

You don't need another channel that does what Klaviyo and Braze already do. You need one that picks up where they stop working.

### The metrics you own — and how FC moves them

**Repeat Purchase Rate**
DTC industry average: ~28% (Shopify benchmark). Email-driven repeat lift typically tops out at +3–5 pp before fatigue. FC re-exposes customers ~7,000 times/year *during* the replenishment window — when the product is actually being used. A conservative +3 pp lift on 10K customers at $50 AOV = **+$150K revenue/year, zero new CAC**.

**Purchase Frequency**
Most DTC brands sit at 1.4–1.8 orders / customer / year. The bottleneck isn't desire — it's *being remembered at the moment of need*. FC fires segmented reorder triggers exactly when consumption is happening (open the fridge → see the brand → tap to reorder). +0.3 orders / customer / year on a $50 AOV, 10K-customer base = **+$150K revenue, no incremental ad spend**.

**Retention / Churn Rate (Day 30–90)**
The window where most DTC cohorts churn. In that window, the average customer receives ~12 emails (~2.4 actual reads at 20% open) and ~6 SMS (~0.24 clicks at 4% CTR). Same window, FC delivers **~1,200 home-side exposures + segmented TAP triggers** — a ~500× exposure ratio on a surface that survives unsubscribe.

**Customer Lifetime Value (CLV)**
+0.5 reorders / customer × $50 AOV = **+$25 CLV per customer**. On a 10K-customer cohort: **+$250K incremental contribution margin** before any scale.

**Activation Rate**
TAP is a new high-signal lifecycle event — customer-initiated, in-home, segment-attributed. Pipe TAP back into Klaviyo / Braze as a new trigger to unlock re-engagement, upsell, and referral flows your stack can't fire today.

**Email / SMS Open & Click**
Email open rates have dropped ~30% in 5 years (Klaviyo benchmark reports). FC doesn't replace your stack — it covers the customers your stack has already lost.

**Incremental Lift / Holdout**
Test design is built in. Same segment, same offer — half ship with FC, half don't. 90-day cohort window, clean repeat-rate delta. Defensible to your CFO from day one.

