## 4. For CMO / VP Brand / Director of Brand Marketing

### Headline

**Brand equity you can see — every day, in ~7,000 routine moments.**

### Subheadline

NPS, referral, recall — these don't come from louder ads. They come from being **unavoidably familiar** in the customer's daily life.

### The metrics you're accountable for — and how FC moves them

**Brand Recall / Top-of-Mind Awareness**
Mere-exposure research: preference rises with frequency, plateauing around 10–20 contacts *(Zajonc, 1968)*. Display ad average viewable impression: ~1.5 sec, often blocked or skipped. FC: **20+ unblockable, in-home brand moments per day** — the highest-frequency owned brand surface available to a DTC brand today.

**NPS**
NPS gains live in the *between-purchase* window — exactly the silence email can't fill. FC converts that silence into branded utility: usage tips, founder stories, ritual content. The brand becomes part of the routine, not an interruption to it.

**Review Volume & Rating**
A +1 pp lift in review-request conversion on 10K customers = **+100 reviews / quarter** at zero CAC. TAP-triggered review prompts fire *while the customer is using the product* — not 14 days later in a forgotten inbox.

**Referral Rate**
Referral programs typically convert <2% of customers because the prompt is buried in email. FC surfaces the referral CTA in a daily routine moment — same offer, **5–10× more eligible exposures**.

**UGC Rate / Social Engagement**
Customers create when prompted in-context. FC is an in-home, in-routine prompt that meets the customer at the moment of use.

**Loyalty Program Participation**
Most loyalty programs lose 70%+ of signups to post-enrollment invisibility. FC keeps tier status, points, and rewards persistently visible in the kitchen — loyalty becomes an **environment**, not an email.

